      "page_title": "Running Concurrently: gather & TaskGroup",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Sequential vs Concurrent",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "await a(); await b()  # 1s+2s=3s",
            "r = await asyncio.gather(",
            "    a(), b())  # ~max = 2s",
            "# r == [res_a, res_b]",
            "# kw: return_exceptions=True"
          ],
          "note": "results come back in ARGUMENT order"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**Sequential**: `await a(); await b()` takes time(a) + time(b)",
            "Both being `async` does not make them overlap",
            "==gather== runs both at once: about max(time(a), time(b))",
            "Results come back in __argument order__, not finish order",
            "`return_exceptions=True` puts exceptions in the list as values, so the first one isn't raised"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. TaskGroup (3.11+)",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "from asyncio import TaskGroup",
            "async with TaskGroup() as tg:",
            "    t1 = tg.create_task(a())",
            "    t2 = tg.create_task(b())",
            "# exits after ALL tasks finish",
            "print(t1.result(), t2.result())"
          ],
          "note": "one failure cancels the siblings"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`async with asyncio.TaskGroup() as tg: tg.create_task(a())`",
            "The block **waits** until every task is done",
            "One task fails → its ==siblings are cancelled==",
            "The errors are raised together as an ==ExceptionGroup==",
            "Catch them with `except* ValueError:`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. gather vs TaskGroup",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Feature",
            "gather",
            "TaskGroup"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Style",
              "simple",
              "structured"
            ],
            [
              "Result order",
              "argument order",
              "via t.result()"
            ],
            [
              "On failure",
              "others keep running",
              "siblings cancelled"
            ],
            [
              "Cleanup",
              "manual",
              "safe, automatic"
            ],
            [
              "New code",
              "fine",
              "**preferred**"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 4,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "sem = asyncio.Semaphore(10)",
            "async def get(u):",
            "    async with sem:  # max 10 at once",
            "        return await fetch(u)"
          ],
          "note": "not 10,000 sockets at once"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`asyncio.wait(..., return_when=FIRST_COMPLETED)` gives ==(done, pending)== sets for fine-grained control",
            "`as_completed()` yields tasks in the order they __finish__",
            "`asyncio.timeout(5)` or `wait_for(coro, 5)` raise **TimeoutError**",
            "A ==Semaphore== caps fan-out: `async with sem:` around each fetch"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`timeout(s)` wraps a **block**; `wait_for` wraps one awaitable",
            "Both raise ==TimeoutError== on expiry",
            "The inner work is __cancelled__, not left running"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        }
