      "page_title": "Timeouts: timeout() vs wait_for()",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Two Timeout Forms",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with asyncio.timeout(5):",
            "    await slow()        # 3.11+",
            "r = await asyncio.wait_for(",
            "    slow(), 5)",
            "# TimeoutError + inner cancelled"
          ],
          "note": "both CANCEL the inner work"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`timeout(s)` limits a whole ==block== of awaits",
            "`wait_for(aw, s)` limits **one** awaitable",
            "On expiry the inner work is __cancelled__ first",
            "Then ==TimeoutError== is raised to the caller"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Catching a Timeout",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "try:",
            "    async with asyncio.timeout(5):",
            "        await slow()",
            "except TimeoutError:",
            "    use_cached()  # fallback"
          ],
          "note": "catch OUTSIDE the timeout block"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Inside the block, code sees ==CancelledError==, not TimeoutError",
            "The context manager converts it to TimeoutError **on exit**",
            "Since 3.11 `asyncio.TimeoutError` is the builtin `TimeoutError`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. timeout() vs wait_for()",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "timeout()",
            "wait_for()"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Since",
              "**3.11**",
              "early 3.x"
            ],
            [
              "Wraps",
              "a block",
              "one awaitable"
            ],
            [
              "On expiry",
              "==TimeoutError==",
              "==TimeoutError=="
            ],
            [
              "Inner work",
              "cancelled",
              "cancelled"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
