          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`time.sleep`, `requests.get`, sync DB drivers, big file reads **block**",
            "They hold the ==only thread==, so the loop and every task stall",
            "Rule: use async libs like aiohttp/httpx, asyncpg, aiofiles",
            "...or move the blocking call **off** the loop thread"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. asyncio.to_thread (3.9+)",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def status(url):",
            "  r = await asyncio.to_thread(",
            "    requests.get, url, timeout=5)",
            "  return r.status_code  # loop free"
          ],
          "note": "kwargs pass straight through"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Runs fn in the ==default thread pool==",
            "`await` returns fn's result or re-raises its error",
            "Copies ==contextvars== into the worker thread"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. loop.run_in_executor",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()",
            "data = await loop.run_in_executor(",
            "    None, read_big, path)",
            "f = partial(fn, key=val)",
            "await loop.run_in_executor(",
            "    None, f)  # kw via partial"
          ],
          "note": "positional args ONLY"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`None` selects the default ==ThreadPoolExecutor==",
            "Keywords need `functools.partial(fn, key=val)`",
            "Executor returns a `concurrent.futures.Future`",
            "`asyncio.wrap_future` makes it **awaitable** by the loop"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
