      "page_title": "Why CPU-Bound Work Doesn't Speed Up",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. One Thread, One Runner",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "asyncio runs every coroutine on ==one thread==.",
            "At any moment only **one** piece of Python is executing.",
            "CPU work (hashing, parsing, math) never waits, so it never yields.",
            "CPU code in `async def` just adds overhead. **No** speedup."
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def crunch(n):",
            "    return sha_loop(n)  # 1 s CPU",
            "",
            "await asyncio.gather(",
            "    *map(crunch, range(4)))",
            "# ~4 s total, loop frozen"
          ],
